---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const site = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || "https://crosswordmaker.app";
const title = "AI Crossword Maker vs My Crossword Maker — Honest Comparison";
const description =
  "Feature-by-feature comparison of AI Crossword Maker and My Crossword Maker for teachers who need printable worksheets with answer keys. Facts only — no invented ratings.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/vs/my-crossword-maker/"
  jsonLd={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: title,
      description,
      url: `${site}/vs/my-crossword-maker/`,
      inLanguage: "en",
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "AI Crossword Maker", url: site },
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${site}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Comparisons", item: `${site}/vs/` },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "vs My Crossword Maker",
          item: `${site}/vs/my-crossword-maker/`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is AI Crossword Maker a My Crossword Maker alternative?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes for teachers who want AI topic drafts, editable clues, dual-page PDF print with answer keys, and ESL/CEFR presets. My Crossword Maker remains a long-standing classroom maker with a large community library and familiar free/paid tiers — check their site for current plans.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do you invent star ratings or review scores?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. This page lists product capabilities we ship today versus publicly known My Crossword Maker classroom workflows. We do not invent star ratings or fabricated review counts.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
  ]}
>
  <article class="container section prose" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
    <nav class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/vs/">Comparisons</a> / vs My Crossword Maker
    </nav>
    <h1>AI Crossword Maker vs My Crossword Maker</h1>
    <p>
      Searching for a
      <strong>free My Crossword Maker alternative</strong>
      that still works for classroom printables? Both tools help teachers turn vocabulary into a crossword.
      The fit depends on whether you want a large community puzzle library, or a fast AI topic → editable clues → dual-page PDF path.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.92rem;">
      This page compares capabilities we ship today against My Crossword Maker’s well-known classroom maker workflow.
      No star ratings, no invented review counts. Plan details on their side can change — verify on their site.
    </p>

    <h2>Quick verdict</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>My Crossword Maker</strong> when you want a familiar long-running classroom maker, community-shared puzzles, and their established free/paid options.
      </li>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>AI Crossword Maker</strong> when you want topic → AI clue drafts, editable entries, dual-page PDF print (puzzle + answer key), teacher name lines, and ESL/CEFR presets — with a free demo that does not require signup for the first generate+preview.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href="/ai-crossword-maker/"><strong>Try AI Crossword Maker free</strong></a>
      · <a href="/examples/">Browse printable examples</a>
      · <a href="/vs/crossword-labs/">Also compare vs Crossword Labs</a>
      · <a href="/vs/eclipse-crossword/">vs Eclipse Crossword</a>
      · <a href="/vs/discovery-education-puzzlemaker/">vs Discovery Education Puzzlemaker</a>
      · <a href="/vs/armored-penguin/">vs Armored Penguin</a>
      · <a href="/vs/easy-puzzle-maker/">vs Easy Puzzle Maker</a>
      · <a href="/vs/teachers-corner/">vs The Teacher's Corner</a>
      · <a href="/pricing/">See Free vs Pro</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Feature comparison</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            <th scope="col">AI Crossword Maker</th>
            <th scope="col">My Crossword Maker (typical classroom use)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Paste a word list</td>
            <td>Yes — Words / Paste modes</td>
            <td>Yes — core classroom workflow</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>AI topic → words + clues</td>
            <td>Yes — free daily demo quota</td>
            <td>Not the primary path we claim for them here</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Edit clues before print</td>
            <td>Yes — full entry editor</td>
            <td>Yes — in their maker</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Printable PDF + answer key</td>
            <td>Yes — dual-page layout; free PDFs include light branding</td>
            <td>Classroom print / answer-key options exist in their product family — check current plans</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Teacher name / class / date lines</td>
            <td>Yes — name-line presets</td>
            <td>Varies by template / plan; not compared as identical here</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>ESL / CEFR landing presets</td>
            <td>Yes — dedicated ESL + CEFR pages</td>
            <td>General maker; no CEFR-specific product page claimed here</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Community puzzle library</td>
            <td>Curated example seeds + your own cloud saves</td>
            <td>Large community / shared-puzzle reputation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Share play link</td>
            <td>Yes — <code>/p/…</code> (noindex)</td>
            <td>Yes — shareable classroom puzzles (per their product)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Activity packs / batch variants</td>
            <td>Yes — A/B/C pack export (Pro / credits path)</td>
            <td>Batch / premium classroom features may exist on paid tiers — verify on their site</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Price model</td>
            <td>Free demo + Pro subscription + credit packs</td>
            <td>Long-standing free + paid classroom tiers (check their site for current limits)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Where we are intentionally different</h2>
    <p>
      AI Crossword Maker is built for English classroom and ESL printable workflows:
      topic or vocabulary list → editable clues → interlocking grid → print with answer key.
      The language model drafts words and clues only; the program owns grid placement, numbering, validation, entitlements, and billing.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are <strong>not</strong> a daily crossword play portal, and we do not claim professional NYT-style symmetry or cryptic construction.
      We also do not invent search volumes, star ratings, or AggregateRating schema for competitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Try the classroom path</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/ai-crossword-maker/">Generate from a topic</a> (free demo) or <a href="/crossword-maker-from-word-list/">paste a word list</a>.</li>
      <li>Edit clues, then print puzzle + answer key from <a href="/printable-crossword-maker/">Printable</a> or <a href="/crossword-maker-for-teachers/">Teachers</a>.</li>
      <li>
        Reuse a ready science or language seed from
        <a href="/examples/rock-cycle/">rock cycle</a>,
        <a href="/examples/types-of-clouds/">types of clouds</a>, or
        <a href="/examples/antonyms/">antonyms</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Is AI Crossword Maker a My Crossword Maker alternative?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes for teachers who need AI drafts, editable clues, dual-page PDFs with answer keys, and ESL/CEFR presets.
      My Crossword Maker remains a strong option when you want their familiar maker and community library.
    </p>
    <h3>Do you invent star ratings or review scores?</h3>
    <p>
      No. We list product capabilities we ship today versus publicly known My Crossword Maker classroom workflows.
      We do not publish AggregateRating schema or fabricated review counts.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Related:
      <a href="/vs/crossword-labs/">vs Crossword Labs</a>
      · <a href="/vs/eclipse-crossword/">vs Eclipse Crossword</a>
      · <a href="/vs/discovery-education-puzzlemaker/">vs Discovery Education Puzzlemaker</a>
      · <a href="/vs/armored-penguin/">vs Armored Penguin</a>
      · <a href="/vs/easy-puzzle-maker/">vs Easy Puzzle Maker</a>
      · <a href="/vs/teachers-corner/">vs The Teacher's Corner</a>
      · <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-geography-vocabulary-crossword/">Geography vocabulary how-to</a>
      · <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-history-vocabulary-crossword/">History vocabulary how-to</a>
      · <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-math-vocabulary-crossword/">Math vocabulary how-to</a>
      · <a href="/blog/how-to-print-crossword-worksheets/">Print worksheets</a>
      · <a href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
